{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>Upon, I hewed</b> — like \"hewing in a mountain\" (cf. Isaiah 10:15). The meaning is that He killed some of their prophets, who were misleading them so they would not return." "<b>I killed them</b> — because they spoke falsely, saying utterances of their mouth; therefore I too killed by the utterances of My mouth — perhaps Israel will return." "<b>And your judgments go forth as light</b> — like \"and cause your righteousness to go forth as light\" (Isaiah 58:10). And further, because it says \"like the dawn\" — its meaning is certain."], :book :hosea, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Hosea -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/daat/olam_hatanah/mefaresh.asp?book=15&perek=1&mefaresh=ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:50:23.044491345Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}